WEBVTT

00:40:00.561 --> 00:40:02.432
AG: Even if you've never been to space,

00:40:02.456 --> 00:40:05.452
you know the current circumstances
could be a lot worse.

00:40:05.476 --> 00:40:07.587
My wife and I have been
talking with our kids

00:40:07.611 --> 00:40:10.299
about how lucky we are
that grocery stores are still open

00:40:10.323 --> 00:40:11.736
and utilities are still on.

00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:13.136
We feel deep appreciation

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:16.979
for the people who are hard at work
keeping those services going.

00:40:17.003 --> 00:40:19.487
I've been thinking about
how much harder it would be

00:40:19.511 --> 00:40:21.666
to do my job without
the internet or a phone.

00:40:21.690 --> 00:40:24.650
Recording this podcast would be
pretty much impossible.

00:40:25.330 --> 00:40:27.283
As it does with many astronauts,

00:40:27.307 --> 00:40:30.704
being in space broadened Scott's idea
of who his neighbors were.